<article class="env-lemma" id="01XB">
       
      
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01XB">Lemma <span data-tag="01XB">30.2.2</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a scheme. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a quasi-coherent $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module. For any affine open $U \subset X$ we have $H^ p(U, \mathcal{F}) = 0$ for all $p > 0$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      We are going to apply Cohomology, Lemma <a href="/tag/01EW" data-tag="01EW">20.11.9</a>. As our basis $\mathcal{B}$ for the topology of $X$ we are going to use the affine opens of $X$. As our set $\text{Cov}$ of open coverings we are going to use the standard open coverings of affine opens of $X$. Next we check that conditions (1), (2) and (3) of Cohomology, Lemma <a href="/tag/01EW" data-tag="01EW">20.11.9</a> hold. Note that the intersection of standard opens in an affine is another standard open. Hence property (1) holds. The coverings form a cofinal system of open coverings of any element of $\mathcal{B}$, see Schemes, Lemma <a href="/tag/01HS" data-tag="01HS">26.5.1</a>. Hence (2) holds. Finally, condition (3) of the lemma follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/01X9" data-tag="01X9">30.2.1</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>